@page "/"

<PageTitle>Resume Parser &amp; Candidate Ranker</PageTitle>

<div class="container-fluid mt-4">
    <div class="row mb-4">
        <div class="col-12 text-center">
            <h2 class="display-5">Resume Parser &amp; Candidate Ranker</h2>
            <p class="text-muted">
                Upload resumes in <strong>.txt</strong> or <strong>.pdf</strong> format alongside a job description.
                The pipeline parses each resume, scores candidates semantically, and generates tailored
                interview questions for your shortlist.
            </p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="row justify-content-center">
        <div class="col-12">
            <RankingWidget />
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="row mt-5">
        <div class="col-12">
            <div class="alert alert-info" role="alert">
                <h5 class="alert-heading">
                    <i class="bi bi-info-circle me-2"></i>How It Works
                </h5>
                <p class="mb-0">
                    The pipeline runs three stages:
                    <strong>profile extraction</strong> — each resume is parsed by an LLM into a structured
                    profile (name, skills, experience, education);
                    <strong>semantic scoring</strong> — both the job description and each profile are embedded
                    with <code>text-embedding-3-small</code>, and cosine similarity produces a 0–1 relevance score;
                    <strong>interview question generation</strong> — for the top-N candidates, a second LLM pass
                    creates targeted questions grounded in their actual experience and the role requirements.
                </p>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>
